# Reference image for a Tina consumer repo. Documentation, not a working build:
# it is deliberately not buildable as-is, because the parts that vary per
# company — which harness, which activities, which credentials — are the parts
# you have to fill in.
#
# Copy this into your own private repo, replace the marked lines, and build.
#
# One image serves both roles. The dispatcher and the worker are the same
# binary with different args:
#
#   tina dispatch --workflow vul --limit 5
#   tina run --workflow vul --item VUL-123
#
# FROM python:3.12-slim
#
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # 1. Tina itself.
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # Add the [cloudrun] extra only if the dispatcher enqueues Cloud Run jobs.
# RUN pip install --no-cache-dir "tina-cli==0.1.0"
# # RUN pip install --no-cache-dir "tina-cli[cloudrun]==0.1.0"
#
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # 2. The agent harness. Tina does not ship one — it shells out to whatever the
# #    config names. Install exactly one, and make sure its argv matches the
# #    [harnesses.<name>] command in tina.toml.
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # RUN pip install --no-cache-dir pi
# # RUN npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code
#
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # 3. Activities. Tina contains no fetching code: skills are installed at build
# #    time with napoln and read off disk at runtime. Versioning, pinning, and
# #    upgrades are napoln's job.
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COPY napoln.toml ./
# RUN uvx napoln install --target /app/activities
#
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # 4. The tools the agent needs to produce results. Tina never writes a result;
# #    the agent does, with its own tools. This is the container tool surface —
# #    one of Tina's two guardrails — so keep it to what the activities need.
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends git \
# #     && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*
#
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# # 5. Configuration. Credentials come from the environment at run time (see
# #    .env.example) — never bake them into the image.
# # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WORKDIR /app
# COPY tina.toml /app/tina.toml
#
# ENTRYPOINT ["tina"]
# CMD ["dispatch", "--workflow", "vul", "--limit", "5"]
